    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0980" n="860" xml:id="pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">640.0031 Danube/153</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State of a Conversation
                        With the Rumanian Minister (Davila)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-19">May 19, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During the call of the Rumanian Minister today he asked me about the Danubian
                    matter. I told him I had talked it over with Tardieu and Beneš and several
                    others. The Minister said he thought it was important to get Germany in; that
                    Germany needed the help of the rest and they needed Germany; that originally it
                    had been proposed as a Danubian affair, but he had begun to think that the
                    interest of Germany would be important.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">enry</hi>] L. S[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">timson</hi>] </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
